(6525564, 970725, 27108, '<td valign="top">This is a cheapo photoshop effect! ;)  Dont get me wrong, it does make some parts of the picture kind of cool: all the green leaves at the higher part of the photo (around her head level) and down there where she has her feet on, where there its brown)<br/> <br/>But the effect on the girl (lovely girl btw), doesnt look that good. The portrait in its whole, has lots of potential, if treated differently.</td>', 'This is a cheapo photoshop effect! ;)  Dont get me wrong, it does make some parts of the picture kind of cool: all the green leaves at the higher part of the photo (around her head level) and down there where she has her feet on, where there its brown) But the effect on the girl (lovely girl btw), doesnt look that good. The portrait in its whole, has lots of potential, if treated differently.', '2011-09-02 21:05:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525584, 970746, 27108, '<td valign="top">Lovely picture the one at the left, and like how the petal on the center, looks like if its over the photo (but I see this white around, that shouldnt be white. <br/>Then the 3 pictures on black bacground, are cool!, Love those monkeys! ;)<br/>And there is this pic at the right.. kind of unfocused, but amazing smile!<br/> <br/>The model gets a 11 out of 10! Gorgeous! ;) but the composition isnt that much of my taste. And the "Expert Editing" isnt there either. (again, the model, just astonishing beautiful!)</td>', 'Lovely picture the one at the left, and like how the petal on the center, looks like if its over the photo (but I see this white around, that shouldnt be white. Then the 3 pictures on black bacground, are cool!, Love those monkeys! ;)And there is this pic at the right.. kind of unfocused, but amazing smile! The model gets a 11 out of 10! Gorgeous! ;) but the composition isnt that much of my taste. And the "Expert Editing" isnt there either. (again, the model, just astonishing beautiful!)', '2011-09-02 21:12:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525597, 970699, 27108, '<td valign="top">This one is cool! how the face is emerging from the smoke. But the fingers as candlelights, looks a bit to bizarre :( Must hurt to get your fingers burned up, doesnt it? ;)<br/> <br/>Then there are some minors, on the brushing.. (like at the right of index finger, you can see a black area, that should have matched better the "not so black" around. This, may be cause of your screen beeing a tad darker than it should. (cause I believe mine is kind of calibrated, and I see those places where it should have been better).<br/> <br/>pd. try to put more light/luminance on your monitor, and watch again the photo. :)</td>', 'This one is cool! how the face is emerging from the smoke. But the fingers as candlelights, looks a bit to bizarre :( Must hurt to get your fingers burned up, doesnt it? ;) Then there are some minors, on the brushing.. (like at the right of index finger, you can see a black area, that should have matched better the "not so black" around. This, may be cause of your screen beeing a tad darker than it should. (cause I believe mine is kind of calibrated, and I see those places where it should have been better). pd. try to put more light/luminance on your monitor, and watch again the photo. :)', '2011-09-02 21:18:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525606, 969981, 27108, '<td valign="top">I like this one.. kind of! :P Even beeing the mouth a point of attention, my eyes goes to her eyes.. so this is good. The HDR kind of effect, is not to bad either, quite spot on between beeing a bit to much, and not beeing enough, so well done on this!<br/> <br/>Even with all those good things, I would have taken the photo with the camera straight. not like its now, from a corner. (45g angle?), that makes this photo kind of awkward. And maybe the background I would have preferred it darker (or lighter!)</td>', 'I like this one.. kind of! :P Even beeing the mouth a point of attention, my eyes goes to her eyes.. so this is good. The HDR kind of effect, is not to bad either, quite spot on between beeing a bit to much, and not beeing enough, so well done on this! Even with all those good things, I would have taken the photo with the camera straight. not like its now, from a corner. (45g angle?), that makes this photo kind of awkward. And maybe the background I would have preferred it darker (or lighter!)', '2011-09-02 21:26:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525620, 970613, 27108, '<td valign="top">Someone commented on mine, that my model was kind of scary looking! :P but then, this one must have terrorized him/her :P<br/> <br/>I dont like the fact that you just put a wall texture over her, dont know... havent been a fan of this technique, and used very little if any myself. (though this is better than most of the entries and I predict it to be a Top 10 almost guaranteed!)<br/> <br/>Will love to see other photos with this model, as I believe she is better looking than what we can see here.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Someone commented on mine, that my model was kind of scary looking! :P but then, this one must have terrorized him/her :P I dont like the fact that you just put a wall texture over her, dont know... havent been a fan of this technique, and used very little if any myself. (though this is better than most of the entries and I predict it to be a Top 10 almost guaranteed!) Will love to see other photos with this model, as I believe she is better looking than what we can see here. Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 21:34:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525635, 970568, 27108, '<td valign="top">hmm.. this is quite different of the rest. Love the surroundings! but as a portrait I would like to see her face better. Right now is the stone she''s on that draws my attention to it. and when I watch at her, are the tan of the legs, and muscles/size of her thighs &lt;-- dont get me wrong! I like them in a posiive and sportly way.<br/> <br/>The flexing doesnt look to strong, and the face is the last thing I see in the picture :(   <br/> <br/>but, is she a bicycle rider, yes?<br/> <br/>pd. clean your sensor! ;) that dust mole in the right of the photo, wasnt on my monitor! (hehe.. I checked!) :P</td>', 'hmm.. this is quite different of the rest. Love the surroundings! but as a portrait I would like to see her face better. Right now is the stone she''s on that draws my attention to it. and when I watch at her, are the tan of the legs, and muscles/size of her thighs <-- dont get me wrong! I like them in a posiive and sportly way. The flexing doesnt look to strong, and the face is the last thing I see in the picture :(    but, is she a bicycle rider, yes? pd. clean your sensor! ;) that dust mole in the right of the photo, wasnt on my monitor! (hehe.. I checked!) :P', '2011-09-02 21:42:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525641, 969786, 27108, '<td valign="top">Nice colors, and exotic model.  But my eyes goes to all the bling bling on her top. Kind of annoying me, cause I dont like that! :P <br/> <br/>I miss her eyes are so dark (are her pupils black?)  I hope this picture is part of a bigger session!, would love to see other poses, and framing.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge</td>', 'Nice colors, and exotic model.  But my eyes goes to all the bling bling on her top. Kind of annoying me, cause I dont like that! :P  I miss her eyes are so dark (are her pupils black?)  I hope this picture is part of a bigger session!, would love to see other poses, and framing. Good luck in the challenge', '2011-09-02 21:45:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525657, 970364, 27108, '<td valign="top">This.. half finished morph, is quite disturbing! :P  But for a Challenge I would like to see a "MUCH MORE" elaborated image.<br/> <br/>For the records!... I prefer Halle Berry as Catwoman if I can choose! ;)</td>', 'This.. half finished morph, is quite disturbing! :P  But for a Challenge I would like to see a "MUCH MORE" elaborated image. For the records!... I prefer Halle Berry as Catwoman if I can choose! ;)', '2011-09-02 21:58:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525659, 970684, 27108, '<td valign="top">This portrait is kind of nice.. I like it. If it werent for the growcery and the vacuum/dust cleaner your life would be better! ;)<br/> <br/>a background could be added, but its nice white also. <br/> <br/>pd. its hard in this challenge, the "kind" of "Expert Editing" is so different and vast, that they are good images vs. good images, and its difficult to vote correctly.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This portrait is kind of nice.. I like it. If it werent for the growcery and the vacuum/dust cleaner your life would be better! ;) a background could be added, but its nice white also.  pd. its hard in this challenge, the "kind" of "Expert Editing" is so different and vast, that they are good images vs. good images, and its difficult to vote correctly. Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:02:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525661, 970727, 27108, '<td valign="top">Lovely baby, and cool hat/sombrero ;)<br/> <br/>Would liked a bit more light at her? face, instead of being the background the lighter area of the photo.<br/> <br/>But.. where is the editing in this one? <br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Lovely baby, and cool hat/sombrero ;) Would liked a bit more light at her? face, instead of being the background the lighter area of the photo. But.. where is the editing in this one?  Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:04:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525666, 970692, 27108, '<td valign="top">This could be a much better image! the idea is cool, the framing is cool! the props (jacket/coat, hat, sunglasses, apple, and even the background) are perfect.<br/> <br/>But.. still it doesn''t get my total liking! :(  I believe its a bit to much edited.. it seems the best focused part is the reflection of the apple in the sunglasses and the background (there is something strange!, looks like the apple is on a table, and not in your hands.. in the reflection).<br/> <br/>pd. the model is imported to the background right? I wouldnt do this when she''s wearing a furry coat!, cause it would get almost impossible to get a good job done.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'This could be a much better image! the idea is cool, the framing is cool! the props (jacket/coat, hat, sunglasses, apple, and even the background) are perfect. But.. still it doesn''t get my total liking! :(  I believe its a bit to much edited.. it seems the best focused part is the reflection of the apple in the sunglasses and the background (there is something strange!, looks like the apple is on a table, and not in your hands.. in the reflection). pd. the model is imported to the background right? I wouldnt do this when she''s wearing a furry coat!, cause it would get almost impossible to get a good job done. Good luck in the challenge!', '2011-09-02 22:09:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525671, 970664, 27108, '<td valign="top">This is a very natural portrait, that could score higher if that was the challenge theme. But this challenge was about "Expert Editing", and I cant say I see it here. (maybe some cloning on face?, but thats not "Expert", is it?)<br/> <br/>As a portrait, I would have tried not to get those picture frames in the actual photo framing.<br/> <br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge</td>', 'This is a very natural portrait, that could score higher if that was the challenge theme. But this challenge was about "Expert Editing", and I cant say I see it here. (maybe some cloning on face?, but thats not "Expert", is it?) As a portrait, I would have tried not to get those picture frames in the actual photo framing.  Good luck in the challenge', '2011-09-02 22:12:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525675, 969959, 27108, '<td valign="top">Not bad portrait, and the model reminds me of my sister and cousin when they were at that age. ;)<br/> <br/>I miss a tad focus on pupils (aswell as a little more light on her eyes)<br/> <br/>Cant see a "Expert Editing" in this one either.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Not bad portrait, and the model reminds me of my sister and cousin when they were at that age. ;) I miss a tad focus on pupils (aswell as a little more light on her eyes) Cant see a "Expert Editing" in this one either. Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:14:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525686, 970657, 27108, '<td valign="top">I''ve been trying to analyze this photo for a while, and dont come to any thing but the eyebrows.. dont know, but they seem to dark, when the hair is colored blonde, and everything is nice and light colors. The hand we see better, is kind of strange a little bit.<br/> <br/>Overall this is a good photo!.. but maybe not completly in line with the "Expert Editing", or am I missing something?<br/> <br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I''ve been trying to analyze this photo for a while, and dont come to any thing but the eyebrows.. dont know, but they seem to dark, when the hair is colored blonde, and everything is nice and light colors. The hand we see better, is kind of strange a little bit. Overall this is a good photo!.. but maybe not completly in line with the "Expert Editing", or am I missing something?  Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:18:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525689, 969528, 27108, '<td valign="top">Nice photo and model! I miss some more focus on her eyes, and less on her hand.<br/> <br/>Cant see any "Expert Editing", or even any editing at all though.<br/> <br/> <br/>Good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'Nice photo and model! I miss some more focus on her eyes, and less on her hand. Cant see any "Expert Editing", or even any editing at all though.  Good luck with the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:20:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525696, 970234, 27108, '<td valign="top">This is kind of in the middle of my taste. We got here a female portrait, thats perfect!, the sepia tone, ok!, the narrow dof, hmm.. not quite my liking. But then we got very dark pupils, and there is a competition of attention between the eyes and her teeth, and "NO" it isnt because of the size but of the white and clean they are! It almost seem, you applied a layer with the sepia, and masked or deleted over her teeth. (compare it with the white on her eyes! the teeth are whiter!)<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This is kind of in the middle of my taste. We got here a female portrait, thats perfect!, the sepia tone, ok!, the narrow dof, hmm.. not quite my liking. But then we got very dark pupils, and there is a competition of attention between the eyes and her teeth, and "NO" it isnt because of the size but of the white and clean they are! It almost seem, you applied a layer with the sepia, and masked or deleted over her teeth. (compare it with the white on her eyes! the teeth are whiter!) Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:25:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525698, 970745, 27108, '<td valign="top">hmmm... I love the use of the umbrella, as it gives a nice background motive, and the lines it makes out of your hear are cool aswell.<br/> <br/>But.. no "Extreme Editing" and this picture could have benefit of it.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'hmmm... I love the use of the umbrella, as it gives a nice background motive, and the lines it makes out of your hear are cool aswell. But.. no "Extreme Editing" and this picture could have benefit of it. Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:27:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525703, 970601, 27108, '<td valign="top">Cool idea!, amazing clarity on the model! (and I may say she looks fantastic aswell!) ;)<br/> <br/>But!.. the Puzzle effect is a bit too fake, with too much depth shadow, and the lines dividing are quite disturbing.<br/> <br/>If you just had uploaded the photo without the puzzling, it would get a 8-9 from me (even not having any "Expert Editing" visible, but I believe you did a great face treatment.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'Cool idea!, amazing clarity on the model! (and I may say she looks fantastic aswell!) ;) But!.. the Puzzle effect is a bit too fake, with too much depth shadow, and the lines dividing are quite disturbing. If you just had uploaded the photo without the puzzling, it would get a 8-9 from me (even not having any "Expert Editing" visible, but I believe you did a great face treatment. Good luck in the challenge!', '2011-09-02 22:30:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525705, 970748, 27108, '<td valign="top">Haha.. nice idea on this one! still I miss more sharpness and less grain.<br/> <br/>I believe you could be in the Top10!  (even not having a girl/woman!) ;)<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Haha.. nice idea on this one! still I miss more sharpness and less grain. I believe you could be in the Top10!  (even not having a girl/woman!) ;) Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:34:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525707, 970383, 27108, '<td valign="top">Nice Chair &lt;-- yes I really like it!  and Nice Model!...<br/> <br/>But.. technically speaking, you got some burns on her!.. both shoulders, right thigh, hand and at the head, beside the eye. This burning, should be a NO-NO!.. <br/> <br/>Then I cant see any "Expert Editing" in this photo, so my vote wont be that high. (cant/shouldnt vote on her physique) :P<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Nice Chair <-- yes I really like it!  and Nice Model!... But.. technically speaking, you got some burns on her!.. both shoulders, right thigh, hand and at the head, beside the eye. This burning, should be a NO-NO!..  Then I cant see any "Expert Editing" in this photo, so my vote wont be that high. (cant/shouldnt vote on her physique) :P Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:39:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525709, 970686, 27108, '<td valign="top">This is a nice b&amp;w photo of a nice lady in the US! (or at least is how I see it) <br/> <br/>Technically speaking, I would have a bit more lighting on her, and the framing a bit more open, to see what is all that on her feet (the birds, were a bit hard to recognize), her head (or hair) is out of the pic (over the black frame), and the lamp, has its base cut by the frame aswell.<br/> <br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This is a nice b&w photo of a nice lady in the US! (or at least is how I see it)  Technically speaking, I would have a bit more lighting on her, and the framing a bit more open, to see what is all that on her feet (the birds, were a bit hard to recognize), her head (or hair) is out of the pic (over the black frame), and the lamp, has its base cut by the frame aswell.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2011-09-02 22:42:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6525710, 970285, 27108, '<td valign="top">This I do like pretty much!.. Could be in top3, if mine doesnt get a ribbon. so I prefer that you score at best a 4th position (so I can be in top3) :P<br/> <br/>Good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'This I do like pretty much!.. Could be in top3, if mine doesnt get a ribbon. so I prefer that you score at best a 4th position (so I can be in top3) :P Good luck in the challenge!', '2011-09-02 22:44:34.000000', NULL, 1),
