(6534333, 970086, 96751, '<td valign="top">I don''t think the idea of "expert" editing is to see that it IS editing.  You have created a masterful effect, and in fact, I prefer this version to the original one by a substantial margin.  I love your notes and am grateful that you''ve shared them.  Congrats on your well earned ribbon.  I though it might finish at the top.</td>', 'I don''t think the idea of "expert" editing is to see that it IS editing.  You have created a masterful effect, and in fact, I prefer this version to the original one by a substantial margin.  I love your notes and am grateful that you''ve shared them.  Congrats on your well earned ribbon.  I though it might finish at the top.', '2011-09-09 01:26:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6534340, 970086, 27108, '<td valign="top">Congrats on yellow ribbon! :)<br/> <br/>There you go!, hehe... I still think the same as I commented before. And as I commented to nr.2, is that this image fits better the "Advanced Editing" instead, while the "Expert editing is something more" (at least, as I see it.. though I can be wrong)<br/> <br/>"take a look at the Male Portrait competition (Expert Editing aswell), and see those winners!.. in fact I gave 10''s to nr.1 and nr.2, while a 9 to nr. 3!", in the female portrait  challenge I gave 10''s to nr. 8 and nr. 18, as they fitted better the "expert editing")<br/> <br/>pd. I like much more the other one you posted on the comments!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-09-09 01:13:58.</i></td>', 'Congrats on yellow ribbon! :) There you go!, hehe... I still think the same as I commented before. And as I commented to nr.2, is that this image fits better the "Advanced Editing" instead, while the "Expert editing is something more" (at least, as I see it.. though I can be wrong) "take a look at the Male Portrait competition (Expert Editing aswell), and see those winners!.. in fact I gave 10''s to nr.1 and nr.2, while a 9 to nr. 3!", in the female portrait  challenge I gave 10''s to nr. 8 and nr. 18, as they fitted better the "expert editing") pd. I like much more the other one you posted on the comments!', '2011-09-09 01:26:49.000000', '2011-09-09 02:13:58.000000', 0),
